1
00:00:03,413 --> 00:00:04,513
Won Ho.

2
00:00:04,513 --> 00:00:05,983
Won Ho, can we talk for a minute?

3
00:00:06,513 --> 00:00:07,513
Won Ho.

4
00:00:08,553 --> 00:00:09,553
Move.

5
00:00:10,083 --> 00:00:11,113
Wait, hold on.

6
00:00:12,553 --> 00:00:13,623
Right now,

7
00:00:13,623 --> 00:00:15,193
our employees and the production crew...

8
00:00:15,193 --> 00:00:18,463
are all waiting for you. If you say you're not doing it now,

9
00:00:18,523 --> 00:00:20,093
what about all the production costs?

10
00:00:20,163 --> 00:00:23,463
Then what about me? I'm so furious that you tricked me...

11
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:25,403
that I can't do this show or anything else.

12
00:00:25,463 --> 00:00:27,063
What about me? What am I supposed to do?

13
00:00:27,463 --> 00:00:29,803
Fine, it was all my fault.

14
00:00:29,803 --> 00:00:30,833
I'm so sorry.

15
00:00:31,033 --> 00:00:32,943
I tricked you and made a fool out of you.

16
00:00:32,943 --> 00:00:36,413
That's all my fault. So please, just this once, okay?

17
00:00:36,713 --> 00:00:37,713
No.

18
00:00:38,443 --> 00:00:40,543
Not for me, for our shop.

19
00:00:40,613 --> 00:00:42,853
Stop using the shop as an excuse. This is all about your greed.

20
00:00:42,953 --> 00:00:45,423
This all happened because you were greedy.

21
00:00:47,483 --> 00:00:48,493
So...

22
00:00:49,923 --> 00:00:51,393
you refuse to do it, no matter what?

23
00:00:51,653 --> 00:00:52,963
Yes. Move.

24
00:00:57,733 --> 00:00:58,763
Wait.

25
00:01:00,003 --> 00:01:01,303
I'm not done talking.

26
00:01:01,873 --> 00:01:02,873
What now?

27
00:01:04,703 --> 00:01:05,703
Fine.

28
00:01:06,673 --> 00:01:07,903
I've made my decision.

29
00:01:11,983 --> 00:01:12,983
What was that?

30
00:01:16,483 --> 00:01:17,483
Let's get...

31
00:01:19,523 --> 00:01:21,583
What are you saying? Speak up, I can't hear you.

32
00:01:38,073 --> 00:01:39,773
What did you just do?

33
00:01:42,213 --> 00:01:43,373
Hey, Baek Mi Young.

34
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:46,313
I mean...

35
00:01:56,393 --> 00:01:58,423
At first, I had no idea what it was.

36
00:01:59,823 --> 00:02:02,263
She suddenly pulled something off her finger and threw it.

37
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:06,103
I thought, "No way. She has to be joking."

38
00:02:08,063 --> 00:02:10,033
It was a real Cartier.

39
00:02:10,703 --> 00:02:12,403
If it was a real Cartier...

40
00:02:14,073 --> 00:02:15,243
Doesn't that mean she wants a divorce?

41
00:02:15,413 --> 00:02:18,813
Exactly. She's the one who's in the wrong, not me. So why?

42
00:02:22,153 --> 00:02:23,853
What is this? I didn't order it.

43
00:02:24,013 --> 00:02:26,023
It's from the person over there.

44
00:02:32,363 --> 00:02:34,093
She looks pretty young, doesn't she?

45
00:02:37,893 --> 00:02:38,903
No, thank you.

46
00:02:40,433 --> 00:02:42,073
Please tell them we appreciate it, but we have to decline.

47
00:02:42,503 --> 00:02:44,433
We're in the middle of a serious conversation.

48
00:02:44,833 --> 00:02:46,273
Yes, I understand.

49
00:02:52,383 --> 00:02:55,613
Regardless of who's at fault, if she really asks for a divorce...

50
00:02:56,483 --> 00:02:57,713
What are you going to do then?

51
00:02:58,213 --> 00:02:59,983
Well, then I guess we'll have to.

52
00:03:00,323 --> 00:03:01,323
Really?

53
00:03:01,823 --> 00:03:03,123
You'd actually get a divorce?

54
00:03:03,293 --> 00:03:04,593
Goodness.

55
00:03:05,323 --> 00:03:06,563
That Cartier ring... Darn it.

56
00:03:07,863 --> 00:03:09,633
It was a limited edition.

57
00:03:37,123 --> 00:03:38,123
Hey, are you asleep?

58
00:03:38,893 --> 00:03:40,263
If you're awake, we need to talk.

59
00:04:12,993 --> 00:04:13,993
Wait.

60
00:04:15,733 --> 00:04:16,993
I'm not done talking.

61
00:04:17,863 --> 00:04:18,903
What now?

62
00:04:21,003 --> 00:04:24,273
Fine. I've made my decision.

63
00:04:26,103 --> 00:04:27,373
Let's get a divorce.

64
00:04:28,043 --> 00:04:29,043
What was that?

65
00:04:29,773 --> 00:04:30,773
Let's get a divorce.

66
00:04:31,543 --> 00:04:33,843
I said, let's get a divorce. Let's do it.

67
00:04:35,183 --> 00:04:37,653
What are you saying? Speak up, I can't hear you.

68
00:04:48,963 --> 00:04:50,733
What did you just do?

69
00:05:19,493 --> 00:05:21,163
Hi, everyone.

70
00:05:21,463 --> 00:05:22,693
Hello.

71
00:05:23,133 --> 00:05:24,893
I know you're all curious about what happened...

72
00:05:24,963 --> 00:05:26,333
after we filmed the show yesterday.

73
00:05:27,103 --> 00:05:30,903
To be honest, my husband and I tried really hard.

74
00:05:31,403 --> 00:05:33,043
But right before the shoot,

75
00:05:33,103 --> 00:05:35,673
I came down with a terrible stomach bug,

76
00:05:36,243 --> 00:05:38,573
so filming has been postponed indefinitely.

77
00:05:38,883 --> 00:05:39,983
It's such a shame, isn't it?

78
00:05:40,743 --> 00:05:42,413
I'm upset, but what can I do?

79
00:05:42,583 --> 00:05:44,013
It's all my fault.

80
00:05:44,483 --> 00:05:46,823
I should have taken better care of myself.

81
00:05:48,353 --> 00:05:51,093
Thank you all so much for your concern.

82
00:05:51,553 --> 00:05:53,393
Tomorrow, I'll be introducing...

83
00:05:53,463 --> 00:05:55,933
this year's new Fall-Winter dress line,

84
00:05:55,993 --> 00:05:57,293
and I'll be back to see you all again.

85
00:05:57,463 --> 00:05:59,063
Yes, I'll see you tomorrow.

86
00:05:59,603 --> 00:06:00,633
Bye.

87
00:06:10,213 --> 00:06:11,813
We need to talk.

88
00:06:12,683 --> 00:06:13,683
About what?

89
00:06:14,013 --> 00:06:15,783
Why did you throw your ring yesterday?

90
00:06:16,283 --> 00:06:18,453
Why? Because I don't need it anymore.

91
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,253
What?

92
00:06:20,323 --> 00:06:21,883
I told you clearly yesterday.

93
00:06:22,353 --> 00:06:23,353
I want a divorce.

94
00:06:26,123 --> 00:06:27,893
Baek Mi Young, get over here right now.

95
00:06:27,963 --> 00:06:29,833
Come here. Let's sit down and talk first. Okay?

96
00:06:29,963 --> 00:06:31,093
Forget it. I don't have time.

97
00:06:31,263 --> 00:06:32,303
But...

98
00:06:37,003 --> 00:06:38,033
Darn it...

99
00:06:50,053 --> 00:06:54,683
I was hoping the show would help the company get back on its feet.

100
00:06:55,653 --> 00:06:57,353
It's a real shame.

101
00:06:57,693 --> 00:06:59,093
It's a shame, but there's nothing we can do.

102
00:06:59,663 --> 00:07:01,063
We just have to keep doing our jobs.

103
00:07:02,393 --> 00:07:03,463
Isn't that right, CEO Ji?

104
00:07:03,763 --> 00:07:06,733
Being on TV wasn't a good fit for us anyway.

105
00:07:07,263 --> 00:07:11,533
But we can barely make payroll next month as it is.

106
00:07:13,273 --> 00:07:14,973
Is that CEO Ji's fault?

107
00:07:15,343 --> 00:07:18,213
It's not like CEO Ji is refusing to pay the employees.

108
00:07:18,443 --> 00:07:19,883
No, what I mean is...

109
00:07:22,483 --> 00:07:23,713
Then what about CEO Baek?

110
00:07:24,113 --> 00:07:26,523
Do you think CEO Baek refused to pay everyone,

111
00:07:26,583 --> 00:07:28,153
and that's why she's trying so hard all by herself?

112
00:07:29,053 --> 00:07:30,223
What do you mean, all by herself?

113
00:07:31,053 --> 00:07:33,323
CEO Ji is doing his best too.

114
00:07:34,163 --> 00:07:35,863
Does someone doing their best...

115
00:07:35,933 --> 00:07:38,193
just blow a huge opportunity and run off?

116
00:07:38,363 --> 00:07:39,433
What do you mean, "run off?"

117
00:07:39,503 --> 00:07:40,833
There will be other opportunities.

118
00:07:41,063 --> 00:07:43,273
Director Song, you're speaking way out of line.

119
00:07:44,433 --> 00:07:46,303
Are you pointing at me?

120
00:07:47,603 --> 00:07:49,173
You're going to hit someone if you keep that up.

121
00:07:49,373 --> 00:07:51,173
Seriously, who do you think you're pointing at?

122
00:07:51,243 --> 00:07:53,083
- Unbelievable. - What are you two doing in here?

123
00:07:53,143 --> 00:07:54,813
- I'm right, aren't I? - Seriously, stop it.

124
00:07:54,883 --> 00:07:56,883
CEO Ji.

125
00:07:58,883 --> 00:08:01,723
Yeong Yu, don't you know how to knock?

126
00:08:01,923 --> 00:08:03,123
I'm sorry.

127
00:08:03,353 --> 00:08:06,863
Excuse me, CEO Ji, but I think you'll want to take this call.

128
00:08:07,763 --> 00:08:08,763
For me?

129
00:08:11,393 --> 00:08:14,563
Yes. When did you have in mind?

130
00:08:16,373 --> 00:08:17,433
Yes, that's possible.

131
00:08:18,843 --> 00:08:20,173
Did you have something in mind?

132
00:08:20,943 --> 00:08:24,313
So the person CEO Ji is on the phone with right now...

133
00:08:24,413 --> 00:08:25,743
is really Cheon Man Ju?

134
00:08:26,013 --> 00:08:27,143
Apparently so.

135
00:08:28,613 --> 00:08:31,283
I'm dying to know why Cheon Man Ju called.

136
00:08:31,353 --> 00:08:33,053
Yes, I understand. Okay.

137
00:08:36,093 --> 00:08:37,253
What did Cheon Man Ju say?

138
00:08:37,653 --> 00:08:40,063
She said she's coming here later for a dress consultation.

139
00:08:41,993 --> 00:08:44,763
- Is it really Cheon Man Ju? - The ultimate icon for Gen Z.

140
00:08:45,093 --> 00:08:47,433
- A celebrity's celebrity. - Is this for real?

141
00:08:47,703 --> 00:08:50,903
Cheon Man Ju is really coming here herself?

142
00:08:51,103 --> 00:08:54,243
- Yes. - Someone famous is coming here?

143
00:08:55,403 --> 00:08:56,613
Did you hear that right?

144
00:08:56,773 --> 00:08:58,173
Was it really Cheon Man Ju?

145
00:08:58,343 --> 00:09:00,183
What, am I deaf? How could I mishear that?

146
00:09:00,243 --> 00:09:01,613
I told you it was Cheon Man Ju.

147
00:09:02,043 --> 00:09:04,113
- Incredible. - This is incredible.

148
00:09:04,813 --> 00:09:07,423
- Cheon Man Ju, for real? - Amazing.

149
00:09:07,483 --> 00:09:08,483
This is huge.

150
00:09:08,753 --> 00:09:10,123
Have you ever seen Cheon Man Ju in person?

151
00:09:11,353 --> 00:09:13,293
So, wait, who is Cheon Man Ju?

152
00:09:18,833 --> 00:09:21,233
- Why? - This is a one-time opportunity.

153
00:09:21,763 --> 00:09:24,973
From now on, just use Cheon Man Ju as an excuse with Mi Young.

154
00:09:25,803 --> 00:09:28,573
- What? - Cheon Man Ju, for a dress fitting,

155
00:09:28,803 --> 00:09:31,013
and what's more important to J&White than her right now?

156
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:33,113
The divorce?

157
00:09:33,183 --> 00:09:34,343
Is that more important than Cheon Man Ju?

158
00:09:34,683 --> 00:09:35,683
Than the company?

159
00:09:36,153 --> 00:09:39,583
- Of course not. - Exactly.

160
00:09:40,223 --> 00:09:41,383
For the time being, you need to think...

161
00:09:41,453 --> 00:09:42,453
only about Cheon Man Ju.

162
00:09:42,823 --> 00:09:44,953
At least until her wedding is over.

163
00:09:50,163 --> 00:09:51,833
You know who Cheon Man Ju is, right?

164
00:09:53,663 --> 00:09:54,933
Of course you do.

165
00:09:55,063 --> 00:09:57,903
Anyone in this country who doesn't know her must be a spy.

166
00:09:58,573 --> 00:10:00,543
Then you must have been a spy until this morning.

167
00:10:02,673 --> 00:10:05,913
Anyway, for Cheon Man Ju's sake,

168
00:10:07,383 --> 00:10:09,153
let's put this talk about our divorce on hold.

169
00:10:09,513 --> 00:10:11,653
What does Cheon Man Ju have to do with our divorce?

170
00:10:11,783 --> 00:10:13,653
Of course it has something to do with it.

171
00:10:14,183 --> 00:10:16,023
Look, imagine you're Cheon Man Ju.

172
00:10:16,353 --> 00:10:19,593
You come here for the one dress you'll wear in your lifetime,

173
00:10:19,723 --> 00:10:20,723
and what do you find?

174
00:10:20,723 --> 00:10:22,533
The owners are in the middle of a divorce.

175
00:10:22,663 --> 00:10:24,293
They're fighting over whether to get divorced or not.

176
00:10:24,363 --> 00:10:27,363
How about it? Isn't that kind of a turn-off?

177
00:10:27,703 --> 00:10:29,133
Don't you think that's bad luck?

178
00:10:32,373 --> 00:10:34,403
Mi Young, this is a golden opportunity...

179
00:10:34,473 --> 00:10:35,643
to save the company.

180
00:10:35,713 --> 00:10:37,943
We still have to pay our employees next month.

181
00:10:44,383 --> 00:10:46,223
Cheon Man Ju is here.

182
00:11:02,373 --> 00:11:04,433
- I hope you had an easy trip over. - Hello.

183
00:11:05,533 --> 00:11:07,203
Hello. I'm Cheon Man Ju.

184
00:11:09,243 --> 00:11:12,143
A star doesn't drive herself, so that's not an issue.

185
00:11:14,183 --> 00:11:15,753
It's a bit smaller than I expected.

186
00:11:19,353 --> 00:11:20,353
It's my first time.

187
00:11:26,923 --> 00:11:27,993
Did you see Cheon Man Ju?

188
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:30,093
I did.

189
00:11:30,463 --> 00:11:31,493
What's she like in person?

190
00:11:32,063 --> 00:11:33,063
How should I put it?

191
00:11:33,433 --> 00:11:36,903
Even as a woman, I have to say she has an extraordinary aura.

192
00:11:37,133 --> 00:11:38,633
Gosh, of course.

193
00:11:39,143 --> 00:11:40,743
The man she's marrying...

194
00:11:41,043 --> 00:11:43,113
is one lucky guy.

195
00:11:43,413 --> 00:11:44,413
Goodness.

196
00:11:44,743 --> 00:11:47,243
She had this bag with a jewel on it this big,

197
00:11:47,313 --> 00:11:49,583
- and she was holding it like this. - Really? Incredible.

198
00:11:49,653 --> 00:11:50,913
- And... - Excuse me.

199
00:11:51,553 --> 00:11:55,793
I'm with Cheon Man Ju. Do you happen to know where she is?

200
00:11:56,693 --> 00:11:58,593
Yes, please follow me.

201
00:11:58,653 --> 00:11:59,663
This way.

202
00:12:05,193 --> 00:12:06,303
She looks familiar.

203
00:12:07,203 --> 00:12:08,363
She's my personal photographer.

204
00:12:09,733 --> 00:12:10,803
Hello.

205
00:12:10,873 --> 00:12:12,573
My name is Ahn Hee Ju.

206
00:12:12,703 --> 00:12:14,603
- Yes. - She'll be handling everything...

207
00:12:14,603 --> 00:12:16,513
related to the photography.

208
00:12:16,813 --> 00:12:18,843
I'm a bit particular about my photos,

209
00:12:19,013 --> 00:12:20,583
so I can't just entrust them to anyone.

210
00:12:22,583 --> 00:12:25,953
- These are our sample dresses. - I...

211
00:12:26,553 --> 00:12:28,353
I'm a really big fan of yours, CEO Ji.

212
00:12:29,453 --> 00:12:32,153
I fell completely in love when I saw your dresses.

213
00:12:32,393 --> 00:12:34,923
The dresses are so my style.

214
00:12:36,063 --> 00:12:37,063
Thank you.

215
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:40,663
This is from the J&White signature line...

216
00:12:42,163 --> 00:12:43,233
You see,

217
00:12:43,703 --> 00:12:46,473
I have this huge fantasy about my wedding dress.

218
00:12:47,943 --> 00:12:50,413
A Dress of a Lifetime that's perfect for me.

219
00:12:51,113 --> 00:12:52,173
That's possible, right?

220
00:12:52,243 --> 00:12:53,713
Of course. It's possible.

221
00:12:53,943 --> 00:12:55,643
A perfectly fitting Dress of a Lifetime.

222
00:12:58,783 --> 00:13:00,023
Look at that confidence.

223
00:13:00,083 --> 00:13:02,123
I definitely came to the right place.

224
00:13:03,023 --> 00:13:04,093
Hee Ju.

225
00:13:04,193 --> 00:13:06,063
I think I'll get my party dress here too.

226
00:13:07,063 --> 00:13:08,493
You're having a party too?

227
00:13:08,763 --> 00:13:11,233
It's before the wedding, so of course.

228
00:13:14,003 --> 00:13:16,473
It's in the suite at the Calvin Hotel.

229
00:13:19,103 --> 00:13:20,173
Oh, I'm so sorry.

230
00:13:21,203 --> 00:13:22,273
It's okay.

231
00:13:31,553 --> 00:13:35,123
(CEO Calvin Kim)

232
00:13:39,563 --> 00:13:41,293
Contract with J&White is finalised.

233
00:13:41,793 --> 00:13:44,833
So now all that's left is to deliver the invitation, right, Calvin?

234
00:13:45,093 --> 00:13:46,963
(Cheon Man Ju)

235
00:13:56,073 --> 00:13:58,013
Okay, this is our fitting room.

236
00:13:58,173 --> 00:14:00,483
Feel free to try anything on, and just let me know.

237
00:14:01,443 --> 00:14:02,983
I'm already so excited.

238
00:14:08,723 --> 00:14:09,723
Yes.

239
00:14:14,293 --> 00:14:15,293
Excuse me.

240
00:14:15,323 --> 00:14:17,463
Have we met somewhere before?

241
00:14:17,933 --> 00:14:20,933
- What? - You just look familiar.

242
00:14:21,303 --> 00:14:22,303
Oh, really?

243
00:14:22,573 --> 00:14:24,103
Right? Where have I seen you?

244
00:14:24,403 --> 00:14:25,673
So you do remember.

245
00:14:26,403 --> 00:14:28,603
By the way, did you turn me down on purpose yesterday?

246
00:14:29,143 --> 00:14:30,143
Yesterday?

247
00:14:30,913 --> 00:14:32,043
You don't remember?

248
00:14:32,143 --> 00:14:33,143
The cocktail.

249
00:14:33,413 --> 00:14:34,443
Cocktail?

250
00:14:40,423 --> 00:14:42,053
What is this? I didn't order it.

251
00:14:42,383 --> 00:14:44,393
It's from the person over there.

252
00:14:49,123 --> 00:14:50,493
Right.

253
00:14:51,293 --> 00:14:52,963
But do you know me?

254
00:14:53,363 --> 00:14:56,603
- What? - Why send me a cocktail...

255
00:15:00,703 --> 00:15:02,343
Think carefully.

256
00:15:02,713 --> 00:15:03,913
The restroom is that way, right?

257
00:15:22,663 --> 00:15:23,663
Man Ju.

258
00:15:23,893 --> 00:15:26,233
You're much slimmer than I expected.

259
00:15:26,403 --> 00:15:28,503
Is that an insult or a compliment?

260
00:15:31,033 --> 00:15:33,243
Don't you think my stomach is sticking out a little?

261
00:15:33,803 --> 00:15:36,143
Your stomach? What are you talking about?

262
00:15:36,343 --> 00:15:37,913
You're so slim.

263
00:15:37,973 --> 00:15:40,043
I'm five months pregnant.

264
00:15:40,843 --> 00:15:43,713
It should look a little different from a regular potbelly.

265
00:15:44,253 --> 00:15:45,483
You've never been pregnant, have you?

266
00:15:49,493 --> 00:15:50,693
So you've never been pregnant.

267
00:15:54,393 --> 00:15:57,093
Congratulations on your pregnancy.

268
00:15:57,463 --> 00:15:58,493
But...

269
00:15:59,093 --> 00:16:00,533
if you're pregnant,

270
00:16:01,133 --> 00:16:03,103
instead of a dress with this silhouette,

271
00:16:03,333 --> 00:16:06,403
how about a bell-line dress that falls from here?

272
00:16:06,603 --> 00:16:07,743
- What did you say? - It'd be a different story...

273
00:16:07,743 --> 00:16:08,843
if you were in the first trimester,

274
00:16:08,903 --> 00:16:10,673
but at this stage,

275
00:16:10,743 --> 00:16:13,283
an A-line dress is too tight and could be dangerous.

276
00:16:13,683 --> 00:16:15,483
And as it happens, this season's trend...

277
00:16:15,543 --> 00:16:17,983
is the bell-line dress as well.

278
00:16:18,983 --> 00:16:21,153
Make it an A-line, no exceptions.

279
00:16:23,393 --> 00:16:26,593
- What? - I'll worry about my own stomach.

280
00:16:27,123 --> 00:16:29,533
Just make the waist tight.

281
00:16:29,993 --> 00:16:31,633
Man Ju, I really can't...

282
00:16:33,063 --> 00:16:35,033
You don't like my belly?

283
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:38,903
Whatever.

284
00:16:38,903 --> 00:16:40,273
Just do exactly as I say.

285
00:16:40,973 --> 00:16:43,443
You just care about getting paid anyway, right?

286
00:16:45,073 --> 00:16:46,743
I shouldn't have told you I was pregnant.

287
00:16:48,043 --> 00:16:49,283
My pregnancy is a secret.

288
00:16:49,653 --> 00:16:51,213
Yes, of course.

289
00:16:52,313 --> 00:16:54,083
An A-line dress like this is out of the question.

290
00:16:54,453 --> 00:16:55,853
Revise the dress design.

291
00:16:56,393 --> 00:16:58,153
The waist on this is too tight.

292
00:16:58,553 --> 00:17:00,323
Let's go with a bell-line dress with a more comfortable fit.

293
00:17:00,663 --> 00:17:03,163
Why? Didn't you say Cheon Man Ju wanted this one?

294
00:17:03,363 --> 00:17:05,133
And you still think so after seeing her?

295
00:17:05,493 --> 00:17:07,933
This design isn't flattering for her figure at all.

296
00:17:08,033 --> 00:17:11,833
But a bell-line dress has puffs, so it can cover up her flaws.

297
00:17:11,903 --> 00:17:13,843
That's not our call to make.

298
00:17:13,973 --> 00:17:15,443
Our job is to make the dress the client wants...

299
00:17:15,503 --> 00:17:17,573
and make sure they're satisfied.

300
00:17:17,713 --> 00:17:20,213
Then let's just revise the waistline to be a little higher.

301
00:17:20,283 --> 00:17:21,883
Why are you acting like such an amateur?

302
00:17:22,643 --> 00:17:23,653
Be honest with me.

303
00:17:23,783 --> 00:17:25,253
Is it because Cheon Man Ju disrespected you earlier...

304
00:17:25,313 --> 00:17:26,323
that you're pulling a power trip?

305
00:17:26,383 --> 00:17:27,753
Do you really think I'm on a power trip...

306
00:17:27,823 --> 00:17:28,823
with Cheon Man Ju right now?

307
00:17:29,023 --> 00:17:30,953
If this isn't a power trip, what is it?

308
00:17:31,253 --> 00:17:32,423
Didn't you say yourself...

309
00:17:32,493 --> 00:17:33,823
that the client's needs are the top priority?

310
00:17:34,363 --> 00:17:37,493
It's because I made a mistake with Cheon Man Ju.

311
00:17:37,993 --> 00:17:40,363
- A mistake? - Yes, in the fitting room.

312
00:17:41,163 --> 00:17:43,433
I think she chose this dress rashly because of it.

313
00:17:44,103 --> 00:17:45,703
She's going to regret it later.

314
00:17:45,903 --> 00:17:47,473
She won't regret it at all.

315
00:17:47,803 --> 00:17:50,173
Once she sees the dress I made, she'll love it.

316
00:17:50,573 --> 00:17:51,913
Leave the dress to me.

317
00:17:52,013 --> 00:17:53,983
This is a matter of my pride and philosophy.

318
00:17:54,513 --> 00:17:55,513
So,

319
00:17:55,683 --> 00:17:57,713
you refuse to change the design no matter what, is that it?

320
00:17:57,913 --> 00:17:59,823
I'm absolutely not changing it.

321
00:18:00,123 --> 00:18:02,583
Not without a request from Man Ju. Not even if the sky falls.

322
00:18:07,323 --> 00:18:08,363
Then,

323
00:18:08,663 --> 00:18:10,593
do a corset fitting instead of a zipper fitting.

324
00:18:10,693 --> 00:18:11,693
You can do that, can't you?

325
00:18:11,763 --> 00:18:13,303
What's with you?

326
00:18:13,433 --> 00:18:16,033
Since Man Ju will probably gain more weight,

327
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:17,803
do a corset fitting.

328
00:18:17,873 --> 00:18:19,673
How would you know if Man Ju is going to...

329
00:18:19,743 --> 00:18:21,343
gain weight or not?

330
00:18:21,473 --> 00:18:22,773
I just know.

331
00:18:23,113 --> 00:18:25,273
Man Ju will gain weight even if the sky falls.

332
00:18:25,673 --> 00:18:27,683
So do a corset fitting, understand?

333
00:18:28,683 --> 00:18:29,783
Darn it.

334
00:18:38,753 --> 00:18:40,823
(Punghae Turtle Shrine, Turtle Master)

335
00:18:42,963 --> 00:18:45,063
I pray.

336
00:18:45,393 --> 00:18:48,103
Oh, great spirits, I pray.

337
00:18:51,933 --> 00:18:53,143
Your fate lies across the water.

338
00:18:53,203 --> 00:18:54,343
My gosh.

339
00:18:54,703 --> 00:18:56,073
Yes, that's right.

340
00:18:56,643 --> 00:18:58,143
My son studied abroad.

341
00:18:58,213 --> 00:19:00,513
He went to Milan, Italy, to study fashion.

342
00:19:00,883 --> 00:19:02,743
You're as amazing as they say.

343
00:19:03,283 --> 00:19:05,253
So, what is it you want to ask?

344
00:19:05,483 --> 00:19:08,583
About a baby. My second son's wife.

345
00:19:08,853 --> 00:19:10,853
I want to know when she can have a baby.

346
00:19:12,723 --> 00:19:13,963
All right.

347
00:19:15,663 --> 00:19:17,063
Let's see if a baby is in her future.

348
00:19:27,073 --> 00:19:28,073
It's over.

349
00:19:28,373 --> 00:19:29,513
It has been for a long time.

350
00:19:29,813 --> 00:19:30,813
What?

351
00:19:33,413 --> 00:19:35,443
They were a bad match, blocking each other's fortunes...

352
00:19:35,513 --> 00:19:36,783
and twisting their fates.

353
00:19:38,283 --> 00:19:39,723
They're destined to separate soon.

354
00:19:40,483 --> 00:19:42,453
No, we can't have Won Ho getting a divorce too.

355
00:19:42,523 --> 00:19:45,693
Master, please, take a closer look.

356
00:19:46,463 --> 00:19:48,063
There's no need to look further.

357
00:19:48,263 --> 00:19:50,893
This is all because of your son.

358
00:19:51,033 --> 00:19:54,563
- What about my son? - He committed an unforgivable sin.

359
00:19:54,603 --> 00:19:55,703
That's not true.

360
00:19:55,763 --> 00:19:58,003
My little brother wouldn't hurt a fly.

361
00:19:58,133 --> 00:20:01,043
But his wife isn't exactly blameless either.

362
00:20:01,173 --> 00:20:02,373
Exactly.

363
00:20:02,443 --> 00:20:04,613
Stop beating around the bush...

364
00:20:04,673 --> 00:20:07,583
and tell us straight.

365
00:20:08,083 --> 00:20:09,083
Fine.

366
00:20:10,883 --> 00:20:12,213
Let's see.

367
00:20:12,813 --> 00:20:14,923
Let's take a good, clear look.

368
00:20:29,633 --> 00:20:31,333
Who killed someone?

369
00:20:32,373 --> 00:20:33,603
What did you say?

370
00:20:33,903 --> 00:20:35,373
What? Who killed someone?

371
00:20:36,173 --> 00:20:38,443
Mom, let's go. I think we've seen enough.

372
00:20:38,513 --> 00:20:40,743
- This is ridiculous. - What is this?

373
00:20:40,813 --> 00:20:42,783
Hey. Pay up before you go, you punk.

374
00:20:42,843 --> 00:20:43,913
What? You're calling me a punk?

375
00:20:44,783 --> 00:20:48,423
- Here. Take it, you punk. Let's go. - He's a complete fraud.

376
00:20:48,623 --> 00:20:49,723
"Turtle Master," my foot.

377
00:20:49,793 --> 00:20:51,853
I hope you turn into turtle soup when you die.

378
00:20:55,063 --> 00:20:56,163
- Where did he go? - There.

379
00:20:56,223 --> 00:21:00,603
- Where are you going? Come out. - There.

380
00:21:00,663 --> 00:21:02,003
Come out.

381
00:21:02,063 --> 00:21:03,073
Hey.

382
00:21:03,133 --> 00:21:04,173
- Come out. - Hey, hurry and come out.

383
00:21:04,603 --> 00:21:08,273
- Hey. - I said come out.

384
00:21:08,343 --> 00:21:10,673
- Come out. - Turtle Master, come out.

385
00:21:22,053 --> 00:21:24,553
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

386
00:21:24,623 --> 00:21:27,793
Oh, right. This is an invitation to my party.

387
00:21:28,693 --> 00:21:30,133
Please make time to come,

388
00:21:30,133 --> 00:21:31,433
even if you have to clear your schedule.

389
00:21:34,933 --> 00:21:37,103
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

390
00:21:39,273 --> 00:21:41,603
(Cheon Man Ju's Last Solo Party)

391
00:21:44,043 --> 00:21:46,213
(Location: Calvin Hotel, 6:00pm)

392
00:22:05,793 --> 00:22:07,103
Where were you?

393
00:22:07,263 --> 00:22:08,603
I waited for a long time.

394
00:22:09,003 --> 00:22:10,473
I told you not to come back.

395
00:22:10,703 --> 00:22:13,243
Why are you suddenly treating me like this?

396
00:22:13,743 --> 00:22:15,043
Don't do this to me.

397
00:22:15,403 --> 00:22:16,913
I told you, I'm getting married.

398
00:22:19,643 --> 00:22:21,813
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

399
00:22:22,343 --> 00:22:24,583
You know. I...

400
00:22:25,613 --> 00:22:28,023
I'm really all alone now.

401
00:22:28,653 --> 00:22:31,423
What am I supposed to do without you?

402
00:22:31,793 --> 00:22:32,853
She's pregnant.

403
00:22:35,363 --> 00:22:36,633
Three months along.

404
00:22:39,133 --> 00:22:41,063
I don't want to make you feel any more miserable.

405
00:23:25,243 --> 00:23:27,043
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

406
00:23:29,853 --> 00:23:31,553
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

407
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:41,863
(Cheon Man Ju's Last Solo Party)

408
00:23:41,923 --> 00:23:43,633
(Location: Calvin Hotel, 6:00pm)

409
00:23:53,173 --> 00:23:54,873
Are we going to be here all night?

410
00:23:56,843 --> 00:23:59,443
You must have called me here because you have something to say.

411
00:24:04,583 --> 00:24:06,653
Jeez, this guy.

412
00:24:08,453 --> 00:24:09,683
Ji Won Ho.

413
00:24:12,253 --> 00:24:13,923
Ji Won Ho.

414
00:24:14,863 --> 00:24:17,233
Answer me, Ji Won Ho.

415
00:24:17,593 --> 00:24:19,093
Yes, I'm listening.

416
00:24:19,093 --> 00:24:20,433
Calvin Kim.

417
00:24:21,603 --> 00:24:22,903
My Mi Young.

418
00:24:24,403 --> 00:24:26,743
Can you make her happy?

419
00:24:28,373 --> 00:24:29,503
"My Mi Young?"

420
00:24:32,213 --> 00:24:33,413
Answer me.

421
00:24:33,983 --> 00:24:36,713
Tell me you'll make her happy!

422
00:24:37,313 --> 00:24:39,853
Gosh, I can't just hit a drunk guy.

423
00:24:48,693 --> 00:24:49,793
I...

424
00:24:50,363 --> 00:24:51,733
My Mi Young.

425
00:24:51,733 --> 00:24:53,433
Of course I'm going to make her happy.

426
00:24:53,803 --> 00:24:57,273
I will never hurt Mi Young the way you did.

427
00:24:58,273 --> 00:25:01,173
I'll make her so happy that she won't even remember...

428
00:25:01,243 --> 00:25:02,973
her time with you. I'll make sure of it.

429
00:25:03,573 --> 00:25:04,813
That promise.

430
00:25:05,473 --> 00:25:06,783
Never forget it.

431
00:25:09,283 --> 00:25:10,413
Because I...

432
00:25:11,483 --> 00:25:13,353
will never forget it either.

433
00:25:26,463 --> 00:25:27,533
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

434
00:25:47,323 --> 00:25:48,623
(To CEO Baek Mi Young)

435
00:25:54,263 --> 00:25:56,223
You're going to Cheon Man Ju's party?

436
00:25:56,393 --> 00:25:57,833
Yes, I plan on going.

437
00:25:58,063 --> 00:25:59,903
But isn't it at Calvin Hotel?

438
00:26:00,363 --> 00:26:01,763
Are you sure you'll be okay?

439
00:26:02,903 --> 00:26:05,003
What do you mean, am I okay?

440
00:26:05,303 --> 00:26:06,703
Well,

441
00:26:06,873 --> 00:26:09,943
I'm just worried you might run into Calvin there.

442
00:26:10,013 --> 00:26:14,343
- I'm just worried. - It'd be a little awkward, I guess.

443
00:26:14,443 --> 00:26:16,683
But what can I do? It's all in the past.

444
00:26:17,413 --> 00:26:18,413
I guess so.

445
00:26:19,283 --> 00:26:20,523
Hey.

446
00:26:22,583 --> 00:26:24,623
Calvin got a divorce.

447
00:26:27,123 --> 00:26:28,163
A divorce?

448
00:26:28,563 --> 00:26:29,563
Yes.

449
00:26:30,263 --> 00:26:32,893
There was an article about it a while ago.

450
00:26:36,933 --> 00:26:37,933
Mi Young?

451
00:26:39,003 --> 00:26:40,003
Mi Young?

452
00:26:40,343 --> 00:26:44,213
Oh, here are some beads...

453
00:26:58,023 --> 00:26:59,253
What's wrong with that?

454
00:26:59,893 --> 00:27:02,193
You postponed your divorce because of Cheon Man Ju.

455
00:27:02,263 --> 00:27:04,963
So for her to go to a party Man Ju is throwing...

456
00:27:04,993 --> 00:27:06,033
is only natural, don't you think?

457
00:27:06,363 --> 00:27:08,733
Well, that's true. That's true, but...

458
00:27:09,733 --> 00:27:11,973
Of all places, the party is at...

459
00:27:14,403 --> 00:27:17,813
The party being at the Calvin Hotel is what's bothering you?

460
00:27:18,213 --> 00:27:20,843
Because it's obvious she'll run into Calvin there.

461
00:27:20,943 --> 00:27:23,513
It's been a while since she broke up with Calvin.

462
00:27:24,253 --> 00:27:25,683
And that was before she met you.

463
00:27:25,783 --> 00:27:27,253
They only dated for a short while, right?

464
00:27:30,023 --> 00:27:31,023
What?

465
00:27:31,093 --> 00:27:32,753
Was it more serious?

466
00:27:34,223 --> 00:27:35,893
No, it's nothing like that.

467
00:27:36,193 --> 00:27:38,193
If not, what are you worried about?

468
00:27:38,493 --> 00:27:41,633
Besides, even if Calvin is divorced now,

469
00:27:42,003 --> 00:27:43,973
do you really think he'd hit on her?

470
00:27:44,233 --> 00:27:46,033
Not when you're by her side.

471
00:27:46,533 --> 00:27:47,703
He's divorced?

472
00:27:47,773 --> 00:27:48,773
You didn't know?

473
00:27:49,143 --> 00:27:50,443
When did he get divorced?

474
00:27:50,443 --> 00:27:52,043
Do you even live in this country?

475
00:27:53,243 --> 00:27:54,313
But then,

476
00:27:54,313 --> 00:27:55,583
you didn't even know who Cheon Man Ju was.

477
00:27:55,643 --> 00:27:56,913
Of course you wouldn't know.

478
00:27:59,683 --> 00:28:01,953
So that jerk Calvin got a divorce?

479
00:28:06,693 --> 00:28:07,763
Unbelievable.

480
00:28:17,333 --> 00:28:19,273
Are you happy with the bust length?

481
00:28:19,373 --> 00:28:21,373
Yes. If we add a tulle overlay here,

482
00:28:21,443 --> 00:28:23,343
it'll look more natural, elegant, and beautiful.

483
00:28:32,253 --> 00:28:34,523
Something with floral details like this would suit you too.

484
00:28:34,583 --> 00:28:37,123
This one, or if we put this on the front...

485
00:28:37,253 --> 00:28:39,593
Because it will draw the eyes away from the face.

486
00:28:39,653 --> 00:28:42,163
Will this line work? Now, as for the off-the-shoulder...

487
00:29:01,983 --> 00:29:05,483
Hi, everyone. Yes, hello.

488
00:29:06,313 --> 00:29:09,453
I have some really big news for you all today.

489
00:29:10,093 --> 00:29:12,323
Do you know who visited our shop?

490
00:29:13,423 --> 00:29:16,323
I should wait until we have over 300 viewers to tell you.

491
00:29:17,163 --> 00:29:18,163
We passed it.

492
00:29:18,963 --> 00:29:21,303
The person who visited our shop was...

493
00:29:21,363 --> 00:29:24,303
Drumroll, please. Cheon Man Ju.

494
00:29:25,573 --> 00:29:27,903
For her wedding dress,

495
00:29:27,973 --> 00:29:31,113
Cheon Man Ju chose our very own J&White.

496
00:29:31,173 --> 00:29:32,573
(J&White and Cheon Man Ju are a killer combination.)

497
00:29:32,843 --> 00:29:35,943
I'm so excited to see the dress Cheon Man Ju will be wearing.

498
00:29:36,183 --> 00:29:39,183
We're going to present a truly legendary dress,

499
00:29:39,283 --> 00:29:40,953
so please look forward to it.

500
00:29:41,023 --> 00:29:42,483
(Are you going to Cheon Man Ju's party today?)

501
00:29:42,553 --> 00:29:43,723
(CEO, are you going to the party?)

502
00:29:44,693 --> 00:29:46,423
Cheon Man Ju's party?

503
00:29:46,893 --> 00:29:48,893
(You have to tell us all about it. Can't wait for the pictures.)

504
00:29:49,063 --> 00:29:50,833
Of course. I have to go.

505
00:29:51,793 --> 00:29:52,933
Where do you think you're going?

506
00:29:53,193 --> 00:29:54,763
What kind of married woman just goes to a hotel?

507
00:29:54,833 --> 00:29:56,063
Are you out of your mind?

508
00:29:57,703 --> 00:29:59,403
My husband is so old-fashioned.

509
00:30:00,643 --> 00:30:01,803
Well then, I'll tell you all about it...

510
00:30:01,803 --> 00:30:04,273
when I'm back. He's not angry.

511
00:30:05,013 --> 00:30:06,413
What do you think you're doing?

512
00:30:06,473 --> 00:30:07,913
And you? Are you crazy?

513
00:30:07,983 --> 00:30:09,413
Thinking of going to the Calvin Hotel?

514
00:30:09,413 --> 00:30:10,653
What about the Calvin Hotel?

515
00:30:10,713 --> 00:30:12,253
What's wrong with going to the Calvin Hotel?

516
00:30:12,313 --> 00:30:14,883
Have you already forgotten what kind of person Calvin is?

517
00:30:15,053 --> 00:30:17,093
He cheated on you with another woman,

518
00:30:17,153 --> 00:30:18,823
got that other woman pregnant,

519
00:30:18,893 --> 00:30:20,493
and then married her.

520
00:30:20,893 --> 00:30:23,323
And Calvin recently got divorced.

521
00:30:23,393 --> 00:30:24,763
When I heard that jerk got divorced,

522
00:30:24,833 --> 00:30:26,193
why did I get such a bad feeling?

523
00:30:26,263 --> 00:30:28,563
- I just got a chill down my spine. - So what's your point?

524
00:30:28,633 --> 00:30:29,963
I said I'm going to the Calvin Hotel.

525
00:30:30,033 --> 00:30:31,933
Did I say I was going to a hotel with Calvin?

526
00:30:33,903 --> 00:30:36,043
Who knows? That jerk might approach you again.

527
00:30:36,103 --> 00:30:38,013
What if he tries to harm you?

528
00:30:38,073 --> 00:30:40,073
- What if? - Geez.

529
00:30:40,243 --> 00:30:41,513
What? Harm me?

530
00:30:42,013 --> 00:30:43,953
Isn't this a complete double standard?

531
00:30:44,453 --> 00:30:46,813
- Double standards? - Yes, double standards.

532
00:30:47,323 --> 00:30:49,923
Whatever harm Calvin could possibly do to me now,

533
00:30:49,923 --> 00:30:51,923
compared to how you've torn my heart out all this time,

534
00:30:51,993 --> 00:30:53,253
it would be a drop in the bucket.

535
00:30:53,453 --> 00:30:56,063
- Baek Mi Young. - Stop meddling in my business.

536
00:30:56,123 --> 00:30:57,833
Mind your own business.

537
00:31:02,563 --> 00:31:03,703
Darn it.

538
00:31:12,143 --> 00:31:13,273
Hello.

539
00:31:16,643 --> 00:31:19,653
- Little Dumplings. Hi. - Hi.

540
00:31:19,713 --> 00:31:23,083
You all know today's my party, right?

541
00:31:23,153 --> 00:31:24,323
(Today's dress is going to be legendary.)

542
00:31:24,393 --> 00:31:26,223
Stop telling me how pretty I am.

543
00:31:27,063 --> 00:31:28,063
In a few hours,

544
00:31:28,123 --> 00:31:30,563
this place is going to be completely packed.

545
00:31:30,893 --> 00:31:34,033
I'm just so excited.

546
00:31:35,163 --> 00:31:37,703
Oh, my. Ms. Lin Zhao Ming.

547
00:31:39,173 --> 00:31:42,443
Gosh, being invited to a party like this,

548
00:31:42,503 --> 00:31:45,443
I'm so happy I could die, don't you think?

549
00:32:00,993 --> 00:32:02,693
(Are you okay? This is insane.)

550
00:32:04,993 --> 00:32:08,763
Surprise. Were you surprised?

551
00:32:09,303 --> 00:32:11,933
I wanted to express with my whole body...

552
00:32:12,003 --> 00:32:14,843
that I'm so happy I could just fall over.

553
00:32:16,173 --> 00:32:19,473
Okay, my Little Dumplings. I'll see you all later.

554
00:32:19,943 --> 00:32:22,783
- Bye. - Bye.

555
00:32:22,913 --> 00:32:24,613
- Bye. - See you again.

556
00:32:26,153 --> 00:32:28,183
I'm so dumbfounded.

557
00:32:28,523 --> 00:32:30,593
I was in the middle of a live stream,

558
00:32:30,693 --> 00:32:32,523
and he just burst out of the room...

559
00:32:32,593 --> 00:32:34,393
and started yelling, "Are you crazy? Going to the Calvin Hotel?"

560
00:32:35,563 --> 00:32:37,533
He was just going completely ballistic.

561
00:32:37,693 --> 00:32:40,133
Seriously. I couldn't believe it.

562
00:32:40,193 --> 00:32:42,603
Is CEO Ji jealous or something?

563
00:32:42,663 --> 00:32:44,303
Jealous? Don't be ridiculous.

564
00:32:44,403 --> 00:32:46,273
It's like no matter what I do,

565
00:32:46,333 --> 00:32:48,243
he's just dying to sabotage it.

566
00:32:48,943 --> 00:32:50,543
He's the absolute worst.

567
00:32:52,013 --> 00:32:53,013
Oh, yes.

568
00:32:54,343 --> 00:32:55,343
By the way,

569
00:32:55,343 --> 00:32:57,783
- what are you going to wear later? - What?

570
00:32:57,853 --> 00:32:58,853
I mean, Calvin...

571
00:33:00,213 --> 00:33:03,053
No. You're going to Cheon Man Ju's party.

572
00:33:03,123 --> 00:33:04,923
You can't just wear anything.

573
00:33:05,223 --> 00:33:07,723
Well, I have an outfit in mind.

574
00:33:07,993 --> 00:33:09,563
What? What are you going to wear?

575
00:33:09,923 --> 00:33:12,663
- Have you seen me in this before? - Let me see.

576
00:33:15,963 --> 00:33:17,133
No.

577
00:33:17,203 --> 00:33:20,573
- This is too plain. - You think so?

578
00:33:20,643 --> 00:33:21,773
Let's not do that.

579
00:33:21,843 --> 00:33:25,313
Since you're going, you should get all dressed up.

580
00:33:25,413 --> 00:33:27,843
You might run into Calvin.

581
00:33:27,913 --> 00:33:30,453
Just a minute ago, you were worried about me seeing Calvin.

582
00:33:30,513 --> 00:33:32,753
No, what I mean is,

583
00:33:32,813 --> 00:33:34,953
if you're going to run into him anyway,

584
00:33:35,023 --> 00:33:37,293
you should show up looking drop-dead gorgeous.

585
00:33:37,353 --> 00:33:38,493
That's what I'm saying.

586
00:33:38,953 --> 00:33:41,523
Make Calvin sick with regret for letting you go.

587
00:33:42,023 --> 00:33:43,023
What?

588
00:33:45,963 --> 00:33:48,103
Oh, give me a break.

589
00:33:48,603 --> 00:33:50,303
Is she the star of the party or something?

590
00:33:50,373 --> 00:33:52,533
Cheon Man Ju is the one getting married, not her.

591
00:33:52,933 --> 00:33:54,303
What's wrong, man?

592
00:33:55,073 --> 00:33:57,473
What, is she supposed to wear sweats to a party?

593
00:33:57,543 --> 00:33:58,973
What's wrong with sweats?

594
00:33:59,043 --> 00:34:00,413
She was invited because of work.

595
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:02,113
She should just throw something on and go.

596
00:34:02,113 --> 00:34:03,243
Oh, come on.

597
00:34:03,783 --> 00:34:05,083
That's ridiculous.

598
00:34:05,583 --> 00:34:07,823
The more I think about it, the more pissed I get.

599
00:34:07,883 --> 00:34:09,423
Some of us are covered in thread,

600
00:34:09,483 --> 00:34:11,693
working ourselves to the bone, while others get all dolled up...

601
00:34:11,753 --> 00:34:13,423
and just think about going to a party.

602
00:34:15,363 --> 00:34:16,523
This isn't right.

603
00:34:17,633 --> 00:34:18,793
This really isn't right.

604
00:34:20,563 --> 00:34:21,563
Hey.

605
00:34:22,463 --> 00:34:23,663
Hey, where are you going?

606
00:34:23,903 --> 00:34:24,903
Hey.

607
00:34:26,403 --> 00:34:27,703
Oh, seriously.

608
00:34:30,413 --> 00:34:31,413
Oh my gosh.

609
00:34:33,843 --> 00:34:34,983
Oh my...

610
00:34:35,413 --> 00:34:38,413
You brought all the fabric from the shop.

611
00:34:39,853 --> 00:34:40,883
So,

612
00:34:41,553 --> 00:34:42,653
you're telling me...

613
00:34:42,723 --> 00:34:46,993
- to organise all of this today? - Yes. By colour and design,

614
00:34:47,053 --> 00:34:49,023
please organise and sort all of it.

615
00:34:49,363 --> 00:34:51,433
If you focus, it won't even take 3 or 4 hours.

616
00:34:51,493 --> 00:34:52,663
What? Three or four hours?

617
00:34:52,733 --> 00:34:53,863
I told you.

618
00:34:53,903 --> 00:34:55,603
I have plans tonight.

619
00:34:55,663 --> 00:34:57,633
Work comes before your evening plans.

620
00:34:57,633 --> 00:34:59,533
That's why I don't make plans,

621
00:34:59,633 --> 00:35:01,903
- so I can work. - Are you kidding me right now?

622
00:35:01,973 --> 00:35:03,073
So you're not going to work?

623
00:35:03,143 --> 00:35:04,413
Ji Won Ho, what is wrong with you?

624
00:35:04,413 --> 00:35:06,443
You just keep getting more and more petty.

625
00:35:06,513 --> 00:35:08,583
Petty? Are you done talking?

626
00:35:08,643 --> 00:35:10,213
No, I'm not done. What are you going to do about it?

627
00:35:10,283 --> 00:35:11,353
Go on. Say it.

628
00:35:11,413 --> 00:35:13,283
Hey, you're being petty and pathetic.

629
00:35:13,353 --> 00:35:14,783
I'm pathetic? Work first...

630
00:35:14,853 --> 00:35:17,453
- Is working hard pathetic? - You're disgusting.

631
00:35:17,523 --> 00:35:19,253
This is negligence of duty.

632
00:35:19,323 --> 00:35:20,723
Going to that party is work for me.

633
00:35:20,793 --> 00:35:22,263
You don't have time. Get to it.

634
00:35:22,623 --> 00:35:23,663
Hey, you...

635
00:35:27,663 --> 00:35:29,603
I guess you'd better work hard.

636
00:35:32,233 --> 00:35:33,233
Vice President Kang.

637
00:35:34,973 --> 00:35:37,103
Seriously, what's wrong with CEO Ji?

638
00:35:37,213 --> 00:35:38,473
What about CEO Ji?

639
00:35:38,643 --> 00:35:41,443
He just dropped a bombshell on Mi Young.

640
00:35:41,513 --> 00:35:42,513
A work bombshell.

641
00:35:42,683 --> 00:35:44,713
I mean, she's going to Cheon Man Ju's party today.

642
00:35:44,783 --> 00:35:46,453
And he knows that perfectly well.

643
00:35:46,553 --> 00:35:48,683
I mean, he's treating her like Cinderella or something.

644
00:35:49,183 --> 00:35:52,023
Don't you think CEO Ji is being way too spiteful?

645
00:35:52,123 --> 00:35:54,763
I completely understand where CEO Ji is coming from.

646
00:35:55,263 --> 00:35:57,123
- What? - If it were me,

647
00:35:57,193 --> 00:35:58,493
putting everything else aside,

648
00:35:58,563 --> 00:36:00,563
the name of the party venue alone would upset me.

649
00:36:01,433 --> 00:36:02,733
For example, Director Song,

650
00:36:03,263 --> 00:36:06,403
if your ex-husband's name was plastered all over a hotel...

651
00:36:06,473 --> 00:36:08,843
What does my ex-husband have to do with this?

652
00:36:09,403 --> 00:36:10,403
Pardon?

653
00:36:11,673 --> 00:36:13,983
There's zero chance of that happening.

654
00:36:14,743 --> 00:36:17,483
Who would name a hotel the Bong Gu Hotel?

655
00:36:24,553 --> 00:36:25,993
Her ex-husband's name is Bong Gu?

656
00:36:27,623 --> 00:36:30,193
I'm sorry, Director Song.

657
00:37:42,003 --> 00:37:43,133
What are you doing, you jerk?

658
00:37:47,773 --> 00:37:48,943
That scared me.

659
00:37:50,613 --> 00:37:52,243
What a messed-up dream that was.

660
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:55,343
I need to get it together.

661
00:38:30,913 --> 00:38:31,913
Glad you could make it.

662
00:38:33,083 --> 00:38:34,083
Is everything delicious?

663
00:38:41,563 --> 00:38:42,563
It's a pleasure.

664
00:38:43,123 --> 00:38:44,133
Hello.

665
00:38:44,393 --> 00:38:46,163
Oh my, you're here.

666
00:38:50,903 --> 00:38:52,633
This is my fiancé.

667
00:38:54,473 --> 00:38:56,103
Hello. It's a pleasure to meet you.

668
00:38:56,243 --> 00:38:58,313
Yes, my sincerest congratulations on your marriage.

669
00:38:58,513 --> 00:39:00,013
I hope I didn't put you in an awkward position...

670
00:39:00,073 --> 00:39:01,083
by asking you to come.

671
00:39:01,543 --> 00:39:03,113
Not at all. Of course I had to come.

672
00:39:10,623 --> 00:39:11,723
Are you...

673
00:39:12,593 --> 00:39:14,363
looking for someone?

674
00:39:14,663 --> 00:39:16,163
Not at all. No.

675
00:39:16,993 --> 00:39:18,333
Well, then, please enjoy yourself.

676
00:39:19,033 --> 00:39:21,363
- Okay. - Shall we go upstairs?

677
00:39:34,113 --> 00:39:35,783
Hi there, my Little Dumplings.

678
00:39:36,783 --> 00:39:39,583
Okay, this is where I'm having my pre-wedding party.

679
00:39:39,783 --> 00:39:41,783
What do you think of the party decorations?

680
00:39:42,423 --> 00:39:43,783
Isn't it so pretty?

681
00:39:44,353 --> 00:39:46,393
What? You think I'm prettier?

682
00:39:47,393 --> 00:39:48,493
(Cheon Man Ju has the best taste.)

683
00:39:48,593 --> 00:39:50,093
Ta-da.

684
00:39:50,793 --> 00:39:53,393
What do you think of my dress? It's so pretty, right?

685
00:39:54,903 --> 00:39:56,133
But you know what?

686
00:39:56,633 --> 00:39:58,873
The dress I'll be wearing on my wedding day...

687
00:39:58,933 --> 00:40:00,533
is even prettier than this one.

688
00:40:00,603 --> 00:40:01,673
(We want to see the dress.)

689
00:40:01,743 --> 00:40:02,903
(Show us the dress.)

690
00:40:03,103 --> 00:40:04,413
You want to see it now?

691
00:40:05,943 --> 00:40:06,943
Hold on.

692
00:40:12,313 --> 00:40:15,283
Darn it. This is so distracting, I can't work.

693
00:40:20,823 --> 00:40:22,163
CEO Ji.

694
00:40:23,063 --> 00:40:24,463
This is Man Ju.

695
00:40:26,063 --> 00:40:27,363
Yes, Ms. Man Ju.

696
00:40:27,733 --> 00:40:30,433
Is Man Ju's dress finished?

697
00:40:30,903 --> 00:40:31,903
The dress?

698
00:40:33,403 --> 00:40:35,543
Yes, the dress is finished. Why?

699
00:40:37,643 --> 00:40:40,443
Well, I want to try it on soon today.

700
00:40:41,343 --> 00:40:43,243
Quickly.

701
00:40:44,043 --> 00:40:46,283
You want to try on the dress today?

702
00:40:46,813 --> 00:40:49,353
Yes, right now.

703
00:40:49,753 --> 00:40:50,993
Right now?

704
00:40:51,293 --> 00:40:52,293
Yes.

705
00:40:54,323 --> 00:40:57,093
(Cheon Man Ju's Last Solo Party, Location: Calvin Hotel, 6:00pm)

706
00:41:38,303 --> 00:41:39,303
Please just go.

707
00:41:40,473 --> 00:41:42,373
I don't want to make you feel any more miserable.

708
00:41:57,623 --> 00:41:58,623
Mi Young.

709
00:42:03,593 --> 00:42:05,293
Yes. It's been a while.

710
00:42:07,863 --> 00:42:08,933
It really has been a long time.

711
00:42:24,853 --> 00:42:26,553
Delivery for someone here?

712
00:42:31,253 --> 00:42:33,623
Oh, there you are.

713
00:42:34,523 --> 00:42:36,723
Well, long time no see, Mr. Calvin.

714
00:42:42,333 --> 00:42:43,403
He looks scared.

715
00:42:44,933 --> 00:42:46,133
Nothing happened, right?

716
00:42:46,533 --> 00:42:47,573
What do you mean?

717
00:42:48,143 --> 00:42:49,143
Never mind.

718
00:42:49,543 --> 00:42:51,643
Not that it could've happened. Not with so many people watching.

719
00:42:53,073 --> 00:42:54,413
What are you doing here all of a sudden?

720
00:42:54,713 --> 00:42:56,583
- Well... - I ordered it.

721
00:42:59,253 --> 00:43:00,253
Hello.

722
00:43:01,353 --> 00:43:03,023
I had to try on my dress today,

723
00:43:03,083 --> 00:43:04,793
so I pestered CEO Ji about it.

724
00:43:05,953 --> 00:43:06,953
Right now?

725
00:43:07,863 --> 00:43:09,993
That was some fast delivery.

726
00:43:11,193 --> 00:43:12,633
I guess you ride a motorcycle.

727
00:43:12,963 --> 00:43:15,903
Yes. Speed and accuracy are the lifeblood of delivery.

728
00:43:16,333 --> 00:43:18,773
Here you are. Perfectly prepared, just as you ordered.

729
00:43:18,833 --> 00:43:20,433
The special finishing touch is a gift from me.

730
00:43:20,733 --> 00:43:22,843
Oh, I'm so excited.

731
00:43:23,573 --> 00:43:25,513
- Let's go. - What?

732
00:43:25,573 --> 00:43:27,513
Let's go quickly.

733
00:43:28,143 --> 00:43:29,143
Wait...

734
00:43:43,463 --> 00:43:46,063
Can we talk for a minute?

735
00:43:50,063 --> 00:43:51,703
Man Ju, are you almost ready?

736
00:43:52,003 --> 00:43:53,433
I'm ready.

737
00:43:54,973 --> 00:43:56,443
Ta-da.

738
00:43:58,413 --> 00:44:01,313
- What do you think? - It looks amazing on you.

739
00:44:01,483 --> 00:44:02,483
I like it.

740
00:44:03,013 --> 00:44:05,713
But I think the waistline could be more defined.

741
00:44:05,953 --> 00:44:07,313
Something's just not quite right.

742
00:44:07,553 --> 00:44:08,583
But did you not see it?

743
00:44:08,583 --> 00:44:10,423
The special finishing touch I prepared?

744
00:44:10,683 --> 00:44:12,393
Wait a minute.

745
00:44:12,393 --> 00:44:14,423
A finishing touch? There's a finishing touch?

746
00:44:15,223 --> 00:44:16,293
Sure.

747
00:44:23,463 --> 00:44:25,803
- I found it. - That, yes, that's it.

748
00:44:25,873 --> 00:44:27,303
Oh, so this is it. Quick, put it on me.

749
00:44:27,303 --> 00:44:28,473
Okay, I got it.

750
00:44:34,843 --> 00:44:36,043
Hold on, I will do it.

751
00:44:43,723 --> 00:44:45,353
As tight as possible.

752
00:44:46,753 --> 00:44:48,563
There we go.

753
00:44:53,793 --> 00:44:55,663
It's so beautiful.

754
00:44:56,003 --> 00:44:57,263
I'm going to go show this off.

755
00:45:03,543 --> 00:45:04,543
What did you want to say?

756
00:45:05,273 --> 00:45:06,713
The invitation you got from Man Ju.

757
00:45:07,613 --> 00:45:08,613
I was the one who sent it.

758
00:45:09,183 --> 00:45:11,183
You did?

759
00:45:11,913 --> 00:45:12,913
Why?

760
00:45:13,553 --> 00:45:14,553
Because I missed you.

761
00:45:16,753 --> 00:45:17,923
I have really missed you.

762
00:45:19,553 --> 00:45:23,093
You missed me.

763
00:45:26,433 --> 00:45:27,493
So what?

764
00:45:28,933 --> 00:45:32,233
What's going to change just by us looking at each other?

765
00:45:34,943 --> 00:45:35,943
Look,

766
00:45:36,843 --> 00:45:38,873
from now on, just pretend you don't know me.

767
00:45:40,073 --> 00:45:41,083
To me,

768
00:45:41,813 --> 00:45:44,143
you are like someone who doesn't exist.

769
00:45:47,553 --> 00:45:48,653
I'm going to go now.

770
00:45:50,453 --> 00:45:51,453
Are you happy?

771
00:45:54,323 --> 00:45:55,323
Are you?

772
00:46:00,463 --> 00:46:01,503
Of course.

773
00:46:02,633 --> 00:46:03,903
You saw my husband, didn't you?

774
00:46:05,133 --> 00:46:06,133
I'm...

775
00:46:07,843 --> 00:46:09,173
doing very well.

776
00:46:10,543 --> 00:46:11,713
I'm incredibly happy.

777
00:46:22,583 --> 00:46:23,583
CEO Ji.

778
00:46:24,993 --> 00:46:26,593
You don't recognise me?

779
00:46:27,153 --> 00:46:28,163
What?

780
00:46:29,893 --> 00:46:31,063
Take a closer look.

781
00:46:33,763 --> 00:46:34,833
Don't you remember me?

782
00:46:42,243 --> 00:46:43,403
Are you hitting on me?

783
00:46:45,043 --> 00:46:46,043
What?

784
00:46:46,943 --> 00:46:48,183
That's strange.

785
00:46:48,443 --> 00:46:51,013
You look so young. Why are you using such an old-fashioned pickup line?

786
00:46:52,253 --> 00:46:55,523
Look, I'm sorry, but you're not my type at all.

787
00:46:56,583 --> 00:46:59,353
- What? - Stop playing games.

788
00:47:01,123 --> 00:47:03,523
And I'm only saying this because you remind me of my little sister,

789
00:47:04,163 --> 00:47:05,763
but you shouldn't mess with a married man.

790
00:47:05,833 --> 00:47:07,063
You could get into real trouble.

791
00:47:08,333 --> 00:47:09,333
Milan.

792
00:47:11,303 --> 00:47:13,503
- What? - Don't you remember?

793
00:47:14,303 --> 00:47:17,243
Eight years ago, in Milan.

794
00:47:19,473 --> 00:47:20,473
Milan?

795
00:47:29,953 --> 00:47:31,053
If we look at these models,

796
00:47:31,123 --> 00:47:33,523
accessories from the new collection would really make them stand out.

797
00:47:33,593 --> 00:47:36,893
Yes, I agree. The material and the design...

798
00:47:36,963 --> 00:47:39,233
are both important. What do you think?

799
00:47:39,293 --> 00:47:41,263
- I completely agree. - Thank you.

800
00:47:41,363 --> 00:47:42,663
Excuse me, I'm just going to use the restroom.

801
00:47:42,763 --> 00:47:43,763
Of course, go ahead.

802
00:47:57,113 --> 00:47:58,613
Where do you think you're going?

803
00:48:11,263 --> 00:48:13,663
Excuse me, you're Korean, right?

804
00:48:18,803 --> 00:48:19,803
I remember now.

805
00:48:20,233 --> 00:48:23,643
That kid from Milan. No, the pickpocket.

806
